## Round 5 — /ship re-run: Codex review of the round-4 fixes
Run: 2026-08-24, branch issue-36-harness
Scope: the two harness fixes from the prior /ship round were themselves
       reviewed by Codex, which found all three items below.
================================================================

Codex verdict on the previous round: "Both fixes are incomplete."

1. Deadline clamp re-created the timeout bug. `timeout=min(PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS,
   remaining)` still launched a probe with less than the full two-request budget
   whenever the overall deadline was close, killing it mid-flight after Govee may
   already have accepted the verification request. Fixed: refuse to start unless
   the full budget remains, and report `overall_timeout_exceeded`, which is the
   accurate reason.

2. tempfile.gettempdir() was the wrong home for the lock. It honours $TMPDIR, so
   two shells with different values silently took different locks; on Linux it
   also defaults to a world-writable /tmp where another local user can pre-create
   the predictable filename or a symlink at it. Fixed: the lock now lives in
   ~/.cache/govee2mqtt-live-2fa/ (created mode 0700, ownership and non-symlink
   verified at use).

3. Confirmation-gate precedence had regressed. Reading GOVEE_LIVE_ACCOUNT_SHA256
   before the GOVEE_LIVE_CONFIRM check changed which error a doubly-misconfigured
   run reports. Codex confirmed no network-safety bypass. Fixed: confirmation is
   checked first again.

