### Regression proof (each fix reverted in isolation, suite re-run)

  revert deadline refusal -> clamp
    test_probe_refuses_to_start_without_its_full_budget ... FAILED
  revert lock back to tempfile.gettempdir()
    test_lock_path_ignores_tmpdir ... FAILED
  revert confirmation-first ordering
    test_confirmation_gate_is_checked_before_the_account_hash ... FAILED

  All three restored: 21 passed, 0 failed.

The ordering test was added specifically because the first mutation run of that
revert passed — nothing covered it. Stated rather than quietly patched.

### Empirical checks (not inference)

  Two worktrees resolve tempfile.gettempdir() identically on this macOS host
  (/var/folders/hf/.../T, mode 0700, uid 501), which is why the original TMPDIR
  approach appeared to work locally. It is still wrong for the $TMPDIR-override
  and Linux-/tmp cases Codex named, hence the move to ~/.cache.

  Real lock dir after the fix:
    /Users/<user>/.cache/govee2mqtt-live-2fa/<account-hash>.lock
    dir mode 0700, owned by the running user, not a symlink, not world-writable.

  fcntl.flock is per-open-file-description, verified on this host: a second
  RunLock on the same path raises even inside one process. That is what makes
  test_lock_actually_excludes_a_second_holder a genuine mutual-exclusion test
  rather than a path-string comparison.

### Not exercised live

No live Govee/IMAP run this round. All three fixes are on control-flow and
filesystem paths that the recorded live sequence never hit (it had no timeouts,
no concurrent run, and a valid configuration).

### Round 5 addendum — independent coverage audit

A parallel coverage audit of the round-4 delta reached the same conclusions
independently, by manual branch trace plus its own mutation run, and proved one
gap the round-5 fixes did NOT close: main() carries its own copy of the sha256
regex, separate from the one in verify_account_allowlist, and testing the other
copy gives it no protection. Closed with
test_malformed_account_hash_is_rejected_before_locking; mutation-verified by
deleting the guard, which fails that test. Python suite 21 -> 22.

That audit ran against the pre-fix commit while these files were being edited,
so its headline 33% figure describes b931026, not the shipped state. Recorded
here because the finding it produced was real and is now fixed.

ROUND 5 GATES: OK
